# Hypothesis: each 4-cell component of 2s is an L/corner tetromino. Its "corner" cell (elbow) 
# defines a slot. Components of type T-up (rows: top-full, middle-below-center) vs T-down (middle-top-full...).
# Two orientations per type. In output, 3 cells and 1 cells form shapes themselves.
# Demo2: comps: T-up at (0,0): cells rel [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,1)]; T-down at (3,0): [(0,1),(1,0),(1,1),(1,2)].
# Out: 3 at (0,0), 1 at (0,3). Two pieces -> 2 cells. Piece1 (T-up, elbow top-left) -> 3; piece2 (T-down, elbow mid-right?) -> 1.
# Demo3: comps T-up(0,0), T-up(3,2), T-down(4,0). Out: 3@(0,0), 1@(0,3), 1@(2,3).
# Hmm positions differ. Maybe output = union of pieces translated so each fits? Like each piece placed at a distinct spot forming a 2x3 mini-grid?
# Think differently: output 3x6 = each component rendered as its 3x3 bounding box? No—out has only 7 cells total across demos, while components have 4 cells each.
# New idea: output shows, for each pair of adjacent components that TOUCH/DIAGONALLY RELATE, ... let's check touching in input.
for n in range(1,7):
    I=G[f'Demo pair {n} input']; O=G[f'Demo pair {n} output']
    seen=set(); comps=[]
    for r in range(len(I)):
        for c in range(len(I[0])):
            if I[r][c]==2 and (r,c) not in seen:
                st=[(r,c)]; seen.add((r,c)); comp=[]
                while st:
                    y,x=st.pop(); comp.append((y,x))
                    for dy,dx in((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):
                        p=(y+dy,x+dx)
                        if 0<=p[0]<len(I) and 0<=p[1]<len(I[0]) and I[p[0]][p[1]]==2 and p not in seen:
                            seen.add(p); st.append(p)
                comps.append(comp)
    # diagonal adjacency (touching corners)
    pts={(r,c) for r in range(len(I)) for c in range(len(I[0])) if I[r][c]==2}
    diag=[]
    for (a,b) in [(i,j) for i in range(len(comps)) for j in range(i+1,len(comps))]:
        dr=min(abs(p[0]-q[0]) for p in comps[a] for q in comps[b]); dc=min(abs(p[1]-q[1]) for p in comps[a] for q in comps[b])
        diag.append((dr,dc,a,b))
    print(f'demo{n}: comps={len(comps)} diag touches=',diag)
    nz=[(i,j,v) for i,row in enumerate(O) for j,v in enumerate(row) if v]
    print(' outnz=',nz)

